WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Adolf Eichmann

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:04.350
Adolf Eichmann was a thin little man with
bow legs and a hook nose.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.760
In the civilian world he had been viewed as
of no account, a socially awkward loser with

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.330
little to redeem himself.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.340
Having joined the Nazi party, however, his
unquestioning commitment to orders coupled

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:20.021
with his need for ruthless efficiency allowed
him to carve out a career that see him go

00:00:20.021 --> 00:00:24.930
down as one of the greatest mass murderers
in all of human history.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:36.030
In this week’s Biographics, we trace the
life, crimes and death of Adolf Eichmann.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:47.250
Formative Years

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.929
Adolf Otto Eichmann was born in Solingen,
Germany on March 19th, 1906 to book-keeper,

00:00:52.929 --> 00:00:55.589
Adolf Karl Eichmann and his wife Maria.

00:00:55.589 --> 00:01:00.190
The oldest of five children, young Adolf was
a nervous, shy child with few friends.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:04.439
When he was seven years old, his father moved
to Linz to take a job as a commercial manager

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:08.119
for the city’s electrical provider, with
the rest of the family following a year later.

00:01:08.119 --> 00:01:13.170
In Linz, Adolf attended the Kaiser Franz Joseph
secondary school, the same school that Adolf

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.189
Hitler had attended in the 1890’s.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:19.970
He remained an aloof and lonely child and
his parents worried about his lack of social

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:20.970
skills.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.219
His dark complexion and distinctive nose and
ears led to his schoolmates teasing him with

00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:29.030
the nickname ‘der kleine Jude’ – the
little Jew.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.670
Adolf proved to be a mediocre student at best.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.320
By the time he became a teenager he had a
reputation as being difficult and moody, with

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.579
his father having written him off as a no
hoper.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:43.860
With little promise of furthering an education,
he quit school at age fifteen and began to

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.950
train as a mechanic.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.710
But at this, too, he proved a failure.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:51.840
After two frustrating years, he gave up on
this career and took a job as a sales agent

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.140
for a mining company.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.869
This job also lasted for two years, after
which he became a district agent for an oil

00:01:57.869 --> 00:01:58.869
company.

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:03.100
By the age of twenty-five, Eichmann was a
sullen, withdrawn, socially inept little man

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.149
who could still be mistaken for a Jew.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:10.870
He had a stable but uninspiring job that saw
him working around Upper Austria and Salzburg.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:16.440
In 1932, despite never having shown any interest
in political affairs, he joined the National

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.820
Socialist Party.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.690
His association with the party began at the
urging of a friend by the name of Ernst Kaltenbrunner,

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:26.190
who was a party official.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:32.760
Becoming a Nazi

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:39.800
For Eichmann the party gave him an opportunity
to belong to a group and to advance his station

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.800
in life.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.190
More than anything he wanted to be somebody
and to prove to the world that he had value

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.340
as an individual.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.480
In November, 1932 he was accepted into the
ranks of the SS, with his duties involving

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.900
forming part of the protection squad for speakers
at party rallies and guarding the party headquarters

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.900
at Linz.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.040
Meanwhile he continued working for the oil
company.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.290
A few weeks after Hitler became Chancellor
of Germany in January, 1933, Eichmann lost

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.400
his job due to staff cutbacks.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.450
He immediately applied for active SS duty
in Germany.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.870
This was accepted and he proved to be a diligent
follower of orders, rising to the rank of

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.050
Scharfuhrer in just a few months.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:23.330
In November, 1933 he was appointed to the
administrative staff of the Dachau concentration

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.330
camp.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:28.690
At Dachau, Eichmann’s job was to keep a
detailed catalog of all the items that were

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.000
confiscated from incoming Jewish prisoners.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.070
He did the job well but found it to be exceedingly
boring.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:39.460
Around this time, he began to set his mind
to studying and inculcating the basic principles

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.510
of Nazism.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:42.530
In summing up what he had come to believe
he said . . .

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.600
If they had told me that my own father was
a traitor and I had to kill him, I’d have

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.610
done it!

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:52.400
In an attempt to break out of his monotonous
routine at Dachau, in 1934 Eichmann applied

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.040
to join the SD, which was the security service
of the SS.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.530
His application was successful and he was
transferred to the Nazi Party head office

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.570
in Berlin.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.820
He was quickly promoted to the rank of Hauptscharfuhrer.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:11.960
The Jewish Specialist

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:18.040
Eichmann’s job was now to investigate and
create reports on the activities of Jewish

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.870
organizations in Germany.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.940
He threw himself into the work, learning the
basics of the Hebrew language and establishing

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.990
himself as the Nazi party expert on the culture
and history of the Jews.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.810
Around this time, the perennially shy Eichmann
met and fell in love with Veronika Liebl.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.480
After the required vetting to ensure that
she had no Jewish heritage, the couple were

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.850
married on March 21st, 1935.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.670
They would go on to have four sons.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:48.480
In 1937, Eichmann, who now held the rank of
SS Untersturmfuhrer (second Lieutenant) was

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.190
sent on an important mission to the British
Mandate of Palestine.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:56.780
Along with his superior officer, he was there
to investigate the feasibility of German Jews

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:59.340
being forcibly made to migrate to Palestine.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.880
But the mission never got off the ground with
the British refusing them entry into the country.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:07.730
In the wake of the annexation of Austria,
Eichmann moved to Vienna, with the job of

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.850
organizing the local SS.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:15.639
His efficiency in doing so earned him another
promotion, this time to the rank of SS Obersturmfuhrer

00:05:15.639 --> 00:05:17.380
(first lieutenant).

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.880
He was also selected to initiate the Central
Office for Jewish Emigration, whose express

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:28.340
purpose was to force the expulsion of all
Jews from Austria.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:36.220
Expelling the Jews

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.950
Eichmann threw himself into this new role
with his usual zeal.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:43.951
Within eight months, he had stripped the vast
majority of Jews in the country of all of

00:05:43.951 --> 00:05:48.650
their lands and possessions and forced forty-five
thousand to get out.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:52.620
Ominously, a further one hundred and fifty
thousand simply disappeared.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.000
His efficiency greatly impressed his superiors.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.300
With the invasion of Poland on September 1st
,1939 and the subsequent outbreak of war,

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.639
Hitler’s policy towards the Jews changed.

00:06:03.639 --> 00:06:08.030
No longer would they be encouraged to leave
Germany – from now on they would be forcibly

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.030
deported.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:14.150
Jews were to be herded together and sent to
concentration camps situated in newly acquired

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.340
parts of the Reich.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:21.220
In October, 1939, Eichmann was posted to Berlin,
where he worked directly under Gestapo chief,

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:25.760
Heinrich Muller in establishing the nationwide
Central Office for Jewish Emigration.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.560
His first job was to clear specified areas
of Poland of Jews.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:34.850
At the same time, he continued his pet project
of ridding his beloved Vienna of the Jewish

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:35.880
‘problem’.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.980
He selected Nisko, in the far north of Poland,
as the site for a transit camp where the expelled

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.600
Jews would be gathered before sending them
into the harsh Russian wilderness to fend

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.600
for themselves.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.620
Meanwhile, ethnic Germans were being moved
into the areas of Poland that the Jews had

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:51.760
been evicted from.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.669
On December 19th, 1939, Eichmann received
yet another promotion.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:07:01.130
He was now the overall coordinator of Jewish
affairs and evacuation for the entire German

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:02.130
Reich.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:06.280
All deportations to camps in Poland were now
under his ultimate control.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.130
Many thousands of Jews were also being sent
to an area in the east of Poland known as

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.590
the General Government.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:17.460
Eichmann immediately drew up plans to send
600,000 Jews into the General Government,

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:22.080
but these plans were pushed back due to complaints
by authorities in the east who were worried

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.370
that too many Jews would ruin the economy.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:30.040
In the end some 63,000 people were relocated
to the area, with many others dying in transit.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:35.710
All over occupied Europe, Jews were crowded
into ghettos as they waited to be sent away.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:40.460
The conditions in the ghettoes were appalling,
and many people died before they ever set

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.390
foot on a train carriage.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:47.979
In 1940, Eichmann released a plan to resettle
a million people each year in Madagascar.

00:07:47.979 --> 00:07:51.860
His plan had relied on the Luftwaffe conquering
the British in the Battle of Britain, which

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.820
would have enabled the Germans to take control
of the skies over the Atlantic.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:08:02.090
When this failed to happen, the plans for
Operation Madagascar were shelved indefinitely.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:10.460
Killing the Jews

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:15.430
In September of 1941, Eichmann was called
to a meeting with head of the SD, Reinhard

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:20.490
Heydrich, in which he was informed that the
Fuhrer had ordered that all Jews in countries

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:23.550
occupied by Germany were to be put to death.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:27.480
The timeline for this was to swing into action
after the conquest of the Soviet Union.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.460
However, the entry of the United States into
the war following the Japanese attack on Pearl

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.870
Harbor forced a rethink.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:38.029
The extermination of the Jews was to be given
maximum priority.

00:08:38.029 --> 00:08:42.619
In January, 1942, Heydrich called a meeting
of the major players in the Nazi organization

00:08:42.619 --> 00:08:45.189
at Wannsee on the outskirts of Berlin.

00:08:45.189 --> 00:08:50.350
It was during this meeting that an official
policy of Jewish genocide was laid out.

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.899
Heydrich called it the Final Solution to the
Jewish Question.

00:08:53.899 --> 00:08:58.339
Eichmann had prepared for the meeting by creating
lists of the numbers of Jews in each country

00:08:58.339 --> 00:08:59.720
who had to eliminated.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:04.589
Heydrich then appointed him as his right-hand
man, responsible for coordinating all of the

00:09:04.589 --> 00:09:09.010
trains that would be used to carry Jews to
Polish concentration camps.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:13.269
As a result of the constant supply of human
fodder that Eichmann was responsible for,

00:09:13.269 --> 00:09:19.819
the Death Camps at Auschwitz, Dachau, Treblinka
and Buchenwald became 24 hour killing machines.

00:09:19.819 --> 00:09:24.360
Eichmann funnelled Jews and Gypsies from Austria,
Holland, France, Holland, the Baltic States

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.309
and Yugoslavia to their slaughter.

00:09:26.309 --> 00:09:30.339
Often, they were sent first to Warsaw and
other ghettoes in Poland for ‘resettlement’

00:09:30.339 --> 00:09:31.339
further east.

00:09:31.339 --> 00:09:36.259
In a gross example of distorted perception,
Eichmann wrote the following about his work

00:09:36.259 --> 00:09:37.259
. . .

00:09:37.259 --> 00:09:40.930
Jewry was grateful for the chance I gave it
to learn community life at the ghetto.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:45.559
It made an excellent school for the future
in Israel – basically most Jews feel well

00:09:45.559 --> 00:09:48.050
and happy in their ghetto life.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:52.839
As the months passed, the demands placed on
Eichmann to speed up the killing machine increased.

00:09:52.839 --> 00:09:58.999
He was responsible for supplying victims to
a total of 164 camps spread throughout eastern

00:09:58.999 --> 00:09:59.999
Europe.

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:04.750
In attempts to make the process more efficient
he oversaw the enlargement of the death trains.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:08.939
Still, he gave no thought to supplying those
who were crammed into the carriages for weeks

00:10:08.939 --> 00:10:13.889
on end with food or water and many of them
died on the way.

00:10:13.889 --> 00:10:18.009
Eichmann’ organizational ability was also
employed to improve the efficiency of the

00:10:18.009 --> 00:10:19.249
actual killing process.

00:10:19.249 --> 00:10:23.800
He designed the huge windowless rooms and
suggested that they be disguised as shower

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.240
units in order to allay panic.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:31.069
He also pushed for the replacement of the
relatively inefficient carbon monoxide gas

00:10:31.069 --> 00:10:34.639
with the cyanide-based insecticide Zyklon-B.

00:10:34.639 --> 00:10:39.600
We can get an insight into Eichmann’s ruthless
efficiency by an incident which occurred during

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.839
a roundup of Jews in Paris in 1942.

00:10:42.839 --> 00:10:47.769
Seven thousand people were rounded up, 4051
of them being children.

00:10:47.769 --> 00:10:53.139
However, the city powers objected to the deportation
and managed to secure talks with Eichmann.

00:10:53.139 --> 00:10:56.540
The Jews were holed up in a warehouse without
food or water.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:02.699
For six days, Eichmann stared down the French
officials, insisting that every single Jew

00:11:02.699 --> 00:11:05.160
had to be sent east to their deaths.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:10.490
In 1944, Eichmann was transferred to Hungary,
which had recently been overrun by the Nazis.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:15.610
He was tasked with fast tracking the transportation
of Hungarian Jews to the death camps, which

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.160
he did with ruthless efficiency.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:27.639
In just a few months he had condemned more
than 400,000 of them.

00:11:27.639 --> 00:11:32.279
Getting Out

00:11:32.279 --> 00:11:37.699
By early in 1945 it was obvious to many in
the Nazi hierarchy that the game was up.

00:11:37.699 --> 00:11:41.329
With the Russians coming at them from one
side and the Allies closing in from the other,

00:11:41.329 --> 00:11:44.279
the priority for many became personal survival.

00:11:44.279 --> 00:11:47.839
Reinhard Heydrich decided that the time had
come to put an end to the mass extermination

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:52.529
of the Jews and to set about destroying any
evidence of the crimes against humanity that

00:11:52.529 --> 00:11:53.920
he had authorized.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.170
When Eichmann head about this, however, he
was not happy.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:00.880
He decided, of his own volition, to continue,
and even speed up, the killings.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:03.860
But finally, even he saw the writing on the
wall.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.250
His biggest fear seemed to be the prospect
that he, having been commissioned as a reserve

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.250
Untersturmfuhrer in the Waffen-SS which made
him eligible for combat duty, would be sent

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.809
out to the front lines to fight the Russians
or Americans.

00:12:09.809 --> 00:12:13.529
In March, with the Russians pouring into Hungary,
he fled to Austria where he tried to get his

00:12:13.529 --> 00:12:17.269
old friend Ernst Kaltenbrunner to help him
evade capture by the Allies.

00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:21.470
But the intimate involvement that Eichmann
had had with the Jewish slaughter had made

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:25.579
him a dangerous man to associate with and
Kaltenbrunner, who was trying to save his

00:12:25.579 --> 00:12:27.809
own skin, wanted nothing to do with him.

00:12:27.809 --> 00:12:31.019
Shortly thereafter, Eichmann was captured
by the US Army.

00:12:31.019 --> 00:12:34.759
Having given a false name, he was transferred
between several POW camps.

00:12:34.759 --> 00:12:37.980
He was part of a work detail in Cham, Germany
when he escaped.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:43.329
Managing to secure new identity papers, he
took on the identity of Otto Heninger and

00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:46.110
relocated to Luneburg Heath in Lower Saxony.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.949
He found work in the forestry sector.

00:12:48.949 --> 00:12:52.329
Other members of the Nazi hierarchy were not
as fortunate as Eichmann in their attempts

00:12:52.329 --> 00:12:53.589
to evade justice.

00:12:53.589 --> 00:12:57.249
Many of them ended up at the Nuremburg War
trails where they gave detailed evidence about

00:12:57.249 --> 00:13:00.959
the role that Eichmann had played in the systematic
planning and execution of the extermination

00:13:00.959 --> 00:13:01.959
of the Jew of Europe.

00:13:01.959 --> 00:13:05.869
As a result, he became one of the most sought
after Nazi war criminals.

00:13:05.869 --> 00:13:08.699
In 1950, Eichmann relocated to Italy.

00:13:08.699 --> 00:13:13.889
Here he received the assistance of Alois Hudal,
a Roman Catholic bishop who was a Nazi sympathizer

00:13:13.889 --> 00:13:16.350
and had already helped many to get out of
Europe.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.199
Hudal helped Eichmann obtain a humanitarian
passport from the International Committee

00:13:20.199 --> 00:13:24.940
of the Red Cross, along with a fake identification
and landing permit for Argentina.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:29.449
With these documents he was able to secure
an international passport from the Red Cross.

00:13:29.449 --> 00:13:32.369
He now had everything needed to sail for South
America.

00:13:32.369 --> 00:13:43.309
He departed from Genoa on June 17th, 1950
and arrived in Buenos Aires on July 14th.

00:13:43.309 --> 00:13:48.970
Hunted

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:53.480
For the next two years, under the name of
Ricardo Klement, Eichmann worked for a government

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.920
contractor in Tucuman Province.

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:58.680
After two years he felt secure enough to bring
over his wife and sons.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:03.440
They moved to Buenos Aires, where Eichmann
worked in a series of menial jobs before finding

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.129
employment with Mercedes Benz.

00:14:05.129 --> 00:14:10.339
Over the next few years he would employ his
natural organizational skills to rise to the

00:14:10.339 --> 00:14:11.889
position of department head.

00:14:11.889 --> 00:14:16.739
Beginning in 1956, a neo-Nazi fanatic began
interviewing Eichmann at his home with the

00:14:16.739 --> 00:14:19.509
goal of writing a fawning biography.

00:14:19.509 --> 00:14:24.499
For this project, a large and damning collection
of tapes, transcripts and notes were produced.

00:14:24.499 --> 00:14:29.230
Meanwhile a handful of determined Nazi-hunters
were hot on Eichmann’s trail.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:34.639
Prominent among them was former concentration
camp inmate Simon Wiesenthal.

00:14:34.639 --> 00:14:38.699
In 1953, Wiesenthal had found a postcard in
which a former Nazi victim had mentioned seeing

00:14:38.699 --> 00:14:41.329
‘that pig Eichmann’ in Buenos Aires.

00:14:41.329 --> 00:14:44.709
He passed this information on to the Israeli
Consulate in Vienna.

00:14:44.709 --> 00:14:48.009
The American CIA were also aware that Eichmann
was in South America.

00:14:48.009 --> 00:14:52.120
However, the were unwilling to act on the
information for fear of embarrassing themselves.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:56.730
In the post-war years the Americans had employed
a number of Nazis to work on the Manhattan

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:57.730
atomic bomb project.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:02.149
They didn’t want to go near anything that
would allow that information to leak to the

00:15:02.149 --> 00:15:03.149
public.

00:15:03.149 --> 00:15:06.649
Meanwhile Wiesenthal was working with the
Israeli Intelligence Service, MOSSAD, to build

00:15:06.649 --> 00:15:09.089
a picture of Eichmann’s life in Argentina.

00:15:09.089 --> 00:15:14.549
A break came when Eichmann’s second oldest
son got involved with the daughter of a Holocaust

00:15:14.549 --> 00:15:16.759
survivor who had relocated to Argentina.

00:15:16.759 --> 00:15:20.899
The boy began to boast that his father had
worked for Hitler and was, in fact, the brains

00:15:20.899 --> 00:15:24.139
behind the final solution of the Jewish question.

00:15:24.139 --> 00:15:28.360
The girl promptly reported this information
back to her father, who, in turn, informed

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.459
the Israeli authorities.

00:15:29.459 --> 00:15:34.139
MOSSAD sent an operative to Buenos Aires to
confirm Eichmann’s location and identity.

00:15:34.139 --> 00:15:40.399
It was now up to Israeli Prime Minister David
Ben Gurion to decide whether to proceed diplomatically

00:15:40.399 --> 00:15:44.449
or to simply seize Eichmann and bring him
back to Israel to face the music.

00:15:44.449 --> 00:15:48.429
Knowing that the Argentinians had a record
of declining extradition requests involving

00:15:48.429 --> 00:15:52.649
former Nazis, Ben Gurion decided to take Eichmann
by force.

00:15:52.649 --> 00:15:56.999
An eight-man team of MOSSAD operatives was
sent to Argentina to carry out the mission.

00:15:56.999 --> 00:16:02.089
The operation was carried out on May 11th,
1960 as Eichmann was walking home from work.

00:16:02.089 --> 00:16:05.149
Two agents pretended to be working on a car
as he walked past.

00:16:05.149 --> 00:16:08.000
A third agent approached and asked him for
a cigarette.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:13.250
Eichmann eyed the man nervously and, in that
moment, all three agents sprang upon him.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:17.759
One of them, a karate black belt, delivered
a blow to his neck which rendered him unconscious.

00:16:17.759 --> 00:16:21.619
Eichmann was bundled into a car and taken
to a safe house where he was stripped naked

00:16:21.619 --> 00:16:22.709
and examined.

00:16:22.709 --> 00:16:26.920
Under his right armpit the agents found a
partially removed tattoo which confirmed that

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.509
he was member of the SS.

00:16:28.509 --> 00:16:33.049
On May 21st, a heavily sedated Eichmann was
smuggled out of Argentina on a commercial

00:16:33.049 --> 00:16:39.930
flight bound for Israel.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:45.199
Captured

00:16:45.199 --> 00:16:49.019
When Prime Minister Ben Gurion announced that
the most wanted Nazi in the world had been

00:16:49.019 --> 00:16:52.459
captured it caused an international sensation.

00:16:52.459 --> 00:16:56.459
The Argentinians strongly protested the manner
of the abduction, claiming that it had been

00:16:56.459 --> 00:16:58.920
a violation of Argentinian sovereignty.

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:03.749
Ben Gurion replied that Eichmann had been
captured, not by agents of the Israeli government,

00:17:03.749 --> 00:17:06.039
but by individual citizens.

00:17:06.039 --> 00:17:10.850
The trial of Adolf Eichmann began on April
11th, 1961 in Israel’s Beth Ha’am (House

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:12.250
of the People).

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:15.740
Fifteen charges were levelled against him,
including crimes against humanity.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:20.809
The charges encompassed the view that he was
the man in direct control of the entire Nazi

00:17:20.809 --> 00:17:25.990
bureaucratic structure responsible for the
deaths of millions of people before and during

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:26.990
the war.

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:30.480
Eichmann’s trial was broadcast live on TV
stations around the globe.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.389
After listening to the emotional testimony
of Holocaust survivors and others, Eichmann

00:17:34.389 --> 00:17:36.649
didn’t try to deny the facts.

00:17:36.649 --> 00:17:39.590
His sole defense was that he was simply carrying
out orders.

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:40.590
He stated that he . . .

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:44.960
never did anything, great or small, without
obtaining in advance express instructions

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:47.850
from Adolf Hitler or any of my superiors.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:52.520
The trial took fourteen weeks, at the end
of which Eichmann as convicted on all counts.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.710
The sentence was death by hanging.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:58.990
His defence team made an unsuccessful appeal
for clemency which was turned down by new

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.419
Israeli Prime Minister Yitzhak Ben-Zvi.

00:18:00.419 --> 00:18:05.309
The execution was carried out on June 1st,
1962 at Israel’s Ramla prison.

00:18:05.309 --> 00:18:08.399
Eichmann refused the black hood that was offered
to him on the gallows.

00:18:08.399 --> 00:18:09.669
His final words were . . .

00:18:09.669 --> 00:18:10.930
Long live Germany.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:11.970
Long live Austria.

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:13.299
Long live Argentina.

00:18:13.299 --> 00:18:17.740
These are the countries with who I have been
most closely associated and I shall not forget

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.740
them.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.419
I had to obey the rules of war and my flag.

00:18:21.419 --> 00:18:22.779
I am ready.’

00:18:22.779 --> 00:18:46.870
Eichmann’s body was cremated and his ashes
scattered in international waters 

00:18:46.870 --> 00:19:01.390
in 
the Mediterranean Sea.

